KG42.register("rules-6a08319a3e7c096317d4654a",{"id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R020","paper":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R020","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M03","name":"Market payment","process_stage":"settlement","market_meaning":"The internal-price formula distributes the region's total energy cost and income among participants according to the amounts of energy they consume and generate. Scope: BS allocation of the energy sharing region's total energy cost and income over the time horizon.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function settlement.payment under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R020-E001","source":"pricing.local","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R020-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E30","v141-b-g07-ev-08"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"BS allocation of the energy sharing region's total energy cost and income over the time horizon.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E30","v141-b-g07-ev-08"]},"x":[],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R020-P001","symbol":"r_t^retail","meaning":"Retail price offered by the retailer, used in the BS internal buying-price formula (A28) to evaluate the region's total energy cost for importing electricity over the horizon. Scoped to the BS mechanism in Appendix A.2.3.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-08"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R020-P002","symbol":"r_t^export","meaning":"Export price offered by the retailer, used in the BS internal selling-price formula (A28) to evaluate the region's total income from exported surplus energy over the horizon. Scoped to the BS mechanism in Appendix A.2.3.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-08"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R020-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The internal-price formula distributes the region's total energy cost and income among participants according to the amounts of energy they consume and generate. Scope: BS allocation of the energy sharing region's total energy cost and income over the time horizon.","expression":"A28: p_t^buy = r_t^retail * (sum_{t in T_u^+} sum_{n in PA} e_{n,t}^bid) / (sum_{n in PA} sum_{t in T_l^+} e_{n,t}^bid), T_u^+ = { t | sum_{n in PA} e_{n,t}^bid > 0, t in T }, T_l^+ = { t | e_{n,t}^bid > 0, t in T }; p_t^sell = r_t^export * (sum_{t in T_u^-} sum_{n in PA} |e_{n,t}^bid|) / (sum_{n in PA} sum_{t in T_l^-} |e_{n,t}^bid|), T_u^- = { t | sum_{n in PA} e_{n,t}^bid \u003c 0, t in T }, T_l^- = { t | e_{n,t}^bid \u003c 0, t in T }","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R020-P001","v141-c-R020-P002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E30","v141-b-g07-ev-08"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E30","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p13-c2r2__v141-a-M03-participation","page":13,"printed_page":null,"section":"5","anchor_text":"hy of the evaluation indexes. e- not equal to local consumption [16]. BS mechanism a pro rata cost r","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-13.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"BS mechanism a pro rata cost sharing mechanism, in which the income and cost of each participant are proportional to its electricity production and consumption [16]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-08","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p27-c2r2__v141-a-M03-pricing","page":27,"printed_page":"1019","section":"A.2.3","anchor_text":"(A27) r agent under mid-market rate mechanism. energy cost and income evenly throughout the time hor","equation_id":"A28","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-27.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Bill sharing is a mechanism in which all the prosumers share the energy cost and income evenly throughout the time horizon. The energy bids required by the BS mechanism are the same as those in the SDR mechanism as described by Formula (A18). The internal price is calculated by\n\n\\begin{cases} p_t^{buy} = r_t^{retail} \\cdot \\frac{\\sum_{t \\in T_u^+} \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{n,t}^{bid}}{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} \\sum_{t \\in T_l^+} e_{n,t}^{bid}}, & T_u^+ = \\{ t \\mid \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{n,t}^{bid} > 0, t \\in T \\}, T_l^+ = \\{ t \\mid e_{n,t}^{bid} > 0, t \\in T \\} \\\\ p_t^{sell} = r_t^{export} \\cdot \\frac{\\sum_{t \\in T_u^-} \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{n,t}^{bid}|}{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} \\sum_{t \\in T_l^-} |e_{n,t}^{bid}|}, & T_u^- = \\{ t \\mid \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{n,t}^{bid} \u003c 0, t \\in T \\}, T_l^- = \\{ t \\mid e_{n,t}^{bid} \u003c 0, t \\in T \\} \\end{cases}  (A28)\n\nFormula (A28) actually distributes the total energy cost and income of the whole energy sharing region among the prosumers according the amount of energy they consume and generate. Taking the buying price part as an example, r_t^{retail} \\cdot \\sum_{t \\in T_u^+} \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{n,t}^{bid} is the total energy cost of the whole region for importing electricity from the retailer throughout the time horizon, which is divided by \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} \\sum_{t \\in T_l^+} e_{n,t}^{bid}, the sum of each individual prosumer's total positive net energy consumption throughout the time horizon."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"The BS settlement allocation formula (A28) contains derived internal prices p_t^buy/p_t^sell, energy-bid inputs e_{n,t}^bid, and external retailer prices, but no design or operational decision variable of the settlement rule. C.1's V for this rule (pricing.local, settlement.payment) does not include a bidding node for e_{n,t}^bid, so no x object is asserted.","empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M03-participation","v141-a-M03-pricing","v141-a-M03-settlement"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-08","quote":"Formula (A28) actually distributes the total energy cost and income of the whole energy sharing region among the prosumers according the amount of energy they consume and generate."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E30","quote":"BS mechanism a pro rata cost sharing mechanism, in which the income and cost of each participant are proportional to its electricity production and consumption [16]."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"6da34ef80236bfc1434a3bf89683acc455e47095d37fcfc04d4342250cabc9c8","applicability":"formalized","reason":"v141-b-g07-ev-08 provides the BS internal-price formula (A28) and states that the formula distributes the energy sharing region's total energy cost and income among prosumers according to positive/negative net energy. The formula is transcribed as source, preserving the source's T_l^+ and T_l^- set-builder definitions exactly as written. External retailer prices r_t^retail and r_t^export are added as theta because they are fixed inputs in A28; no x is declared because A28 contains derived internal prices and energy-bid inputs, not design or operational decisions of the settlement rule. C.1's V/E are unchanged. B evidence remains unreviewed; v141-b-g07-ev-08 contains a possible typo in T_l^+/T_l^- and an 'evenly' wording that C.1/B should reconcile.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R020-C001","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R020-E001"],"rationale":"C001 is the BS internal-price formula that defines p_t^buy and p_t^sell in pricing.local; the same source states this formula distributes the region's total cost and income, which is the pricing-to-settlement allocation represented by edge E001 to settlement.payment."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R020-P001","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R020-E001"],"rationale":"r_t^retail is an external fixed price input used in the BS internal buying-price formula in pricing.local; because that formula determines the settlement distribution, the existing pricing-to-settlement edge is relevant."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R020-P002","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R020-E001"],"rationale":"r_t^export is an external fixed price input used in the BS internal selling-price formula in pricing.local; because that formula determines the settlement distribution, the existing pricing-to-settlement edge is relevant."}],"revision_requests":["Source formula (A28) in v141-b-g07-ev-08 defines T_l^+ as { t | e_{n,t}^bid > 0, t in T } and T_l^- as { t | e_{n,t}^bid \u003c 0, t in T } without an explicit sum/index over n; the B note flags this as a possible typographical issue. C.1/B should clarify whether T_l^+ and T_l^- are meant to be summed over n or defined per prosumer. The current C.2 expression preserves the source text as written.","The frozen rule's V (pricing.local, settlement.payment) does not include a bidding.demand/bidding.supply node or variable object for e_{n,t}^bid, although A28 uses energy bids as inputs. If variable-level representation of A28 is required, C.1 should add scoped energy-bid variable/parameter objects or a bidding node; C.2 did not invent such nodes or cross-rule reuse.","The same evidence v141-b-g07-ev-08 begins 'all the prosumers share the energy cost and income evenly throughout the time horizon' while its explanation and A28 describe allocation according to positive/negative net energy. C.1/B should reconcile whether 'evenly' is imprecise wording for allocation over the horizon or a separate equal-sharing settlement rule.","B evidence v141-b-g07-ev-08 is unreviewed (source_status unverified) under this experiment; its formula and the T_l^+/T_l^- definitions require B source re-extraction/audit before scientific acceptance."]},"C2_delivery":{"raw_sha256":"4d55e5bdcfdf245112d9f09de00469911e33e95d474e91995270dc18bb1b81a4","delivery_payload_sha256":"e2fa9b7cec1434fcec81a8f96f55e2942543f80b966b8486a4b719cfa406b35c","changes":[{"path":"theta.0.value.kind","before":"symbolic","after":"unspecified","reason":"Variant tag follows supplied value fields; no value, symbol or scientific statement is added, removed or rewritten."},{"path":"theta.1.value.kind","before":"symbolic","after":"unspecified","reason":"Variant tag follows supplied value fields; no value, symbol or scientific statement is added, removed or rewritten."}],"scientific_fields_unchanged":true,"request_graph_sha256":"6da34ef80236bfc1434a3bf89683acc455e47095d37fcfc04d4342250cabc9c8","scientific_correctness_verified":false}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
